<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George Maniakes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1043</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George Maniakes was a Byzantine general of the 11th century. He took Edessa from its Muslim rulers in 1031 and in 1038 led an expedition, with Varangian and Norman troops, that recovered much of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabs">Arabs</a>. Recalled amid court intrigue, he rebelled and was proclaimed emperor by his troops in 1043, but was killed in battle in Macedonia that year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-maniakes.jpg" alt="George Maniakes" width="247" height="433" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown, 13th-century author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Georgios_Maniakes2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
